{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.TannakaKreinReconstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.TannakaKreinReconstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Functor","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.HopfAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Monoidal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Preserves.Finite"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.tannaka_krein_reconstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.tannaka_krein_reconstruction","kind":"axiom","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L181-L192","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:tannaka-krein-reconstruction","label":"prop:tannaka-krein-reconstruction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.universal_property","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.universal_property","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L131-L131","doc":"`@marker` — Universal property: `carrier` is terminal among\nfactorisations of `τ` through Hopf-algebra representations.\n\n**Still a `Prop`-universe field, and knowingly so** — hence the\n`@marker` opt-out of AGENTS.md §3b-tax, which is the corpus's\nvocabulary for a genuinely-open opaque field (\"honestly framed;\ntracked not counted\").  The justification below was written\n2026-09-07 and is VERIFIED, not taken on trust: Mathlib's\n`RepresentationTheory.Rep` is `abbrev Rep (k G : Type u) [Ring k]\n[Monoid G]`, so it is defined for a **monoid**, and there is no\n`Rep k H` for a Hopf algebra `H` to quantify over.  That is also why\n`RepCat` above has to be carried as a field rather than referenced.  Terminality\nquantifies over all such factorisations, and a factorisation is a\nfunctor into `Rep` of another Hopf algebra — the same missing\ninfrastructure, one level up.  Every other field in this structure was\nencodable once the vocabulary was carried; this one is not, because\nwhat would have to be carried is the whole 2-category of\nHopf-algebra representation categories.  Left as the honest gap\nrather than dressed up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.equiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.equiv","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L111-L111","doc":"**The equivalence `C ≃ Rep(carrier)`.**\n\nWas `monoidal_equiv : Prop`, a field typed with the *universe* `Prop`,\nso the instance chose the proposition and `True` discharged it.  An\nequivalence is DATA; it is now `CategoryTheory.Equivalence`.\n\n**Scope, and it is a real weakening of the name**: this is an\nequivalence of CATEGORIES, not of *monoidal* categories.  Stating the\nmonoidal upgrade needs a monoidal structure on `RepCat`, which is\ndownstream of the `Rep`-for-Hopf-algebras gap above.  The field is\nnamed `equiv` rather than `monoidal_equiv` so the type and the name\nagree; the monoidal half is what remains open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instRepCat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instRepCat","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Category structure on `Rep(carrier)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.RepCat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.RepCat","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The representation category `Rep(carrier)`.\n\nA field, not a reference: Mathlib has `Rep k G` for a group `G` and\n**not** `Rep k H` for a Hopf algebra `H`, so there is nothing to point\nat.  Carrying it is what lets the equivalence below be stated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instHopfAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instHopfAlgebra","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Hopf algebra structure (adds antipode S). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instBialgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instBialgebra","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Bialgebra compatibility (Δ and ε are algebra maps). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instCoalgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instCoalgebra","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Coalgebra structure (comul Δ, counit ε). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instAlgebra","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L84-L84","doc":"k-algebra structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.instRing","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Ring structure on the carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.carrier","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Carrier of the reconstructed Hopf algebra End⊗(τ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TannakaKreinReconstruction","kind":"structure","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/tannaka-krein-reconstruction.lean#L68-L131","doc":"The output of Tannaka–Krein reconstruction: a k-algebra A\ncarrying a `HopfAlgebra k A` structure, together with the\nmonoidal equivalence C ≃ Rep(A) and the universal property.\n\nThe carrier `A` and its `HopfAlgebra` instance are concrete\nMathlib structures.  The equivalence is stated as `Prop`\npending Mathlib infrastructure for `Rep` of a Hopf algebra. ","signatureChunk":0}]}